<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;With the // or ?? delimiters the m at the beginning is optional. &lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That was true until about 8 years ago. [doc://perlop#m?PATTERN?msixpodualngc|Now]:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;In the past, the leading &lt;c&gt;m&lt;/c&gt; in &lt;c&gt;m?PATTERN?&lt;/c&gt; was optional, but omitting it would produce a deprecation warning. As of v5.22.0, omitting it produces a syntax error. If you encounter this construct in older code, you can just add &lt;c&gt;m&lt;/c&gt;.&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;small&gt;&lt;i&gt;Typo fix&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/small&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</doctext>
